  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Fakes in pairs – weight shift and hide the ball",
  "description": "Players pair up with one ball per pair, spread over the ice. Attacker A skates with the ball towards X, who defends at half pace to start with. Practise two fakes:\n\nFake 1 – weight shift: A shifts their weight to one side as if to go past there. When X follows, A quickly shifts back and goes past on the other side. Fake 2 – hide the ball: A pulls the ball back and hides it behind the skates, turns side-on to X, shields the ball with the body and skates past.\n\nSwap roles after 4–5 tries. Progression: X defends for real, or A has to carry the ball over a line behind X. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Sell the fake with the whole body – shoulders and head should \"lie\" too."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Fake at the right distance, about a stick length from the defender."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Accelerate as soon as you are past."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "When you hide the ball, keep your body between the defender and the ball."
    }
  ],
